.TH OROC 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc \- command line interface for Oro Runtime projects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc [SUBCOMMAND] [options] [<project\-dir>]
oroc [SUBCOMMAND] \-h
oroc help [query...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
oroc is the main command line interface for Oro Runtime projects.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
search commands, options, and platform notes
.TP
\fBbuild\fR
build project
.TP
\fBlist\-devices\fR
get the list of connected devices
.TP
\fBinit\fR
create a new project (in the current directory)
.TP
\fBinstall\-app\fR
install app to the device
.TP
\fBprint\-build\-dir\fR
print build path to stdout
.TP
\fBrun\fR
run application
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
inspect configuration values and docs
.TP
\fBenv\fR
print relevant environment variables
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
run an MCP server for agent tooling
.TP
\fBsetup\fR
install build dependencies
.TP
\fBversion\fR
inspect or bump project version
.TP
\fBversions\fR
print Oro CLI/runtime and dependency versions
.TP
\fBupdate\fR
update tooling (keys, manifests, bundles)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBORO_DEBUG\fR
enable debug mode (like \-D)
.TP
\fBORO_VERBOSE\fR
enable verbose logs (like \-V)
.TP
\fBORO_LOG_NO_COLOR\fR
disable colored log output
.TP
\fBORO_LOG_JSON\fR
enable structured JSON logs on stdout
.TP
\fBORO_LOG_FILE\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.TP
\fBORO_ALLOW_EXEC\fR
allow external exec during builds
.TP
\fBORO_ENABLE_SANITIZERS\fR
enable ASan/UBSan on desktop builds
.TP
\fBNO_ANDROID\fR
source bootstrap: disable only Android work when non\-empty
.TP
\fBNO_IOS\fR
source bootstrap: disable only iOS/iOS Simulator work when non\-empty
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
print help message
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR
print install path
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-version\fR
print program version
.TP
\fB\-q, \-\-quiet\fR
hint for less log output
.TP
\fB\-V, \-\-verbose\fR
enable verbose output (can be global)
.TP
\fB\-D, \-\-debug\fR
enable debug output (can be global)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
disable colored log output
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
enable structured JSON logs on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
Run 'oroc <subcommand> \-\-help' for subcommand\-specific flags, examples, and platform notes. Use 'oroc help <query>' to search commands, options, examples, and workflow notes by topic. 'oroc <subcommand> \-\-json' emits structured command results when that subcommand supports it. The global 'oroc \-\-json <subcommand>' form is reserved for JSON log streaming. Use '\-\-log\-file=<path>' when you need machine\-readable stdout plus a separate log stream. NO_ANDROID and NO_IOS are independent presence flags for building the runtime source tree; they do not select an application target for 'oroc build \-\-platform'. Values such as 0 and false are non\-empty and still disable the named target.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc init my\-app\fR
create a starter Oro project in ./my\-app
.TP
\fBoroc run .\fR
run the app rooted at the current directory
.TP
\fBoroc build \-\-platform=ios \-\-prod .\fR
build a production iOS artifact from the current project
.TP
\fBoroc config \-\-describe meta.version\fR
inspect documentation for a single configuration key
.TP
\fBoroc help ios signing\fR
search for commands and notes related to iOS signing and provisioning
.SH UPDATE TOOLING
.TP
\fBoroc update keygen\fR
generate an Ed25519 keypair for signing update manifests
.TP
\fBoroc update init\fR
scaffold a manifest JSON file
.TP
\fBoroc update server\fR
run an update server over HTTP/TCP/UDP
.TP
\fBoroc update info\fR
query update servers or static manifests over HTTP/TCP/UDP
.TP
\fBoroc update sign\fR
sign a manifest JSON file and emit a sidecar signature
.TP
\fBoroc update verify\fR
verify a manifest JSON file + signature using a public key
.TP
\fBoroc update bundle\fR
build a tar archive from a directory suitable as an update artifact
.TP
\fBoroc update extract\fR
extract an update bundle tar archive into a directory
.TP
\fBoroc update validate\fR
validate a manifest.json file against the update manifest schema shape
